        "comments": "The assembly mPhoVit2.hap1.1 is based on 40x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project\n(https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. This genome has been assembled using PacBio and Hi-C data and phased. The result is two curated haplotypes. The X and Y chromosomes were identified based on their single-copy status in the diploid assembly, with the X also identified by synteny with Pusa sibirica (GCA_028975605.1).\nThe exact order and orientation of the scaffolds on are uncertain on: Chromosome Y (12,542 ? 19,560 Kbp).",
